Take words like "military style" and "assault weapon" often used to describe a rifle like the AR-15 (you can legally own in RSA). Think about the purpose here to conflate and mislead:

(1) It is a semi-automatic - no military uses it - it cannot shoot burst or automatic mode;
(2) It can look like a military weapon to the untrained, but isn't near something like a M-16 in terms of technical military functionality (see 1); 
(3) Assault weapon - is lexicon that rose to prominence during a short "assault rifle" ban that characterized rifles that had 3 out of 5  (if I recall) cosmetic characteristics as "assault weapons" in response to mass shootings. It is not a technical term or related to its lethality which is comparable to a hunting rifle (hunting rifles being generally of higher muzzle velocity and range but slower rate of fire - +/- 20s difference for 100 rounds)
